  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohan Lal vs State Of Rajasthan Through Pp on 17 January, 2018 Author: Pankaj Bhandari Bench: Pankaj Bhandari High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Miscellaneous Bail No. 17941 / 2017 Mohan Lal S/o Kapoor Chand B/c Vaishaya, R/o Kalyana Mohalla Kaman P.S. Kaman Distt. Bharatpur. ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan Through P.P. ----Respondent ____________________________________________________",
    "facts": "Petitioner has filed this anticipatory bail application under Section 438 Cr.P.C. 2. F.I.R. No. 221/17 was registered at Police Station Kaman Distt. Bharatpur for offence under Sections 420, 272 of I.P.C. and Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "3. It is contended by counsel for the petitioner that the offence under Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 as well as offence under Section 272 of I.P.C. is bailable and Section 420 of I.P.C. was added to make it non bailable offence. 4.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. It is contended by counsel for the petitioner that the offence under Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 as well as offence under Section 272 of I.P.C. is bailable and Section 420 of I.P.C. was added to make it non bailable offence. 4.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
